        "results_interpretation": "The pooled analysis of four studies assessing the association between zinc exposure and breast cancer survival yields an effect size of 0.82, with a wide 95% confidence interval ranging from 0.43 to 1.55. This broad interval includes the null value, and the association is not statistically significant, indicating that zinc exposure is not associated with improved breast cancer survival based on current evidence. Moreover, the heterogeneity is substantial (I\u00b2 = 86.22%), suggesting that there is considerable variability among the included studies, which may affect the reliability of the pooled estimate. Therefore, further research is warranted to clarify these findings due to the observed inconsistency between studies."
